# Code standards

## General

- Match surrounding style, naming, and error handling
- Minimal diffs; no drive-by refactors
- Env-driven config; no hardcoded hosts in server code (browser URLs use `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` at build time)

## Python (backend, runner, trame-viewer)

- FastAPI routers; typed models where the file already uses them
- Paths via `JOBS_ROOT` env, not literals scattered across services
- Log failures with enough context for job id / path debugging

## TypeScript (frontend)

- Functional React components; colocate job/viewer logic with existing pages
- Viewer and AI bridges: extend `trameBridge.ts` / `aiChat.ts` rather than new ad-hoc message types
- Parse AI XML only through established tags in `backend/services/ccs/prompt.py` contract

## Docker

- Service changes require `docker-compose.yml` (and `docker-compose.aws-dev.yml` if env/volumes/ports change)
- Document new env vars in `docs/development/setup.md` and `.env.example`
